description:
Scaffold a new workspace crate `pkix-identity` for cert-side identity matching. Decision per `.3`: option B (separate crate, not inline in profiles or pkix-chain).

## Deliverable

A new top-level workspace crate `pkix-identity/`:

- **`Cargo.toml`**: name `pkix-identity`, version `0.1.0`, edition 2021, `rust-version = "1.73"`, license `Apache-2.0 OR MIT`, repository pointer, `publish = true`.
- **`no_std`** (matches `pkix-path` discipline). `#![cfg_attr(not(test), no_std)]` in lib.rs. `extern crate alloc` where needed.
- **Dependencies**: `x509-cert` (no default features, for `Certificate`), `der` (for parsing extensions), `idna` (for IDN A-label/U-label conversion). NO dep on pkix-path, pkix-chain, or pkix-profiles (one-way dep flow).

## Public API skeleton

```rust
// pkix-identity/src/lib.rs

#![cfg_attr(not(test), no_std)]
extern crate alloc;

use x509_cert::Certificate;

/// Parsed server identity: DNS hostname or IP literal.
pub struct ServerName<'a> { /* ... */ }

impl<'a> ServerName<'a> {
    pub fn dns_name(name: &'a str) -> Result<Self, IdentityError> { unimplemented!() }
    pub fn ip_address(ip: &'a str) -> Result<Self, IdentityError> { unimplemented!() }
}

/// Parsed RFC 5322 / RFC 8398 mailbox.
pub struct MailboxName<'a> { /* ... */ }

impl<'a> MailboxName<'a> {
    pub fn parse(mailbox: &'a str) -> Result<Self, IdentityError> { unimplemented!() }
}

/// Identity-binding errors.
#[non_exhaustive]
pub enum IdentityError {
    NotYetImplemented,
    MalformedInput,
    NoMatchingSan,
    MissingSan,
    // ... fleshed out in .11/.12
}

/// RFC 6125 §6.4 hostname binding: does leaf cert authorize `name`?
pub fn verify_dns_name(cert: &Certificate, name: &ServerName<'_>) -> Result<(), IdentityError> {
    Err(IdentityError::NotYetImplemented)
}

/// RFC 5280 §4.2.1.6 + RFC 8398 mailbox binding: does leaf cert authorize `mailbox`?
pub fn verify_mailbox(cert: &Certificate, mailbox: &MailboxName<'_>) -> Result<(), IdentityError> {
    Err(IdentityError::NotYetImplemented)
}
```

`NotYetImplemented` is explicit (not `panic!`) so callers in this window get a loud, structured signal. `.11` and `.12` fill in the bodies.

## Workspace integration

- **Workspace `Cargo.toml`**: add `pkix-identity` to `members` array.
- **AGENTS.md**: add to the "Adjacent / specialized crates" list with a one-line description and scope-discipline note.
- **`pkix-identity/README.md`**: short — what this crate does, what's in scope, what's deliberately NOT in scope (name constraints stay in pkix-path; DN canonicalization stays in pkix-path; public suffix list NOT enforced — caller's responsibility).

## Scope discipline (load-bearing)

This crate has high risk of "what doesn't go in here?" scope creep. Discipline:

**In scope:**
- `ServerName` parsing (DNS hostname + IP literal).
- `MailboxName` parsing (RFC 5322 + RFC 8398 SmtpUTF8Mailbox via otherName).
- `verify_dns_name` (RFC 6125 §6.4 matching).
- `verify_mailbox` (RFC 5280 §4.2.1.6 + RFC 8398 matching).
- IDN A-label/U-label normalization via `idna` crate.
- Internal helpers: wildcard matching, case folding, IP byte compare.

**Out of scope:**
- Name constraints matching (lives in `pkix-path/src/lib.rs:2190` as `dns_name_matches_constraint` — different semantics: constraint check, not target match).
- DN canonicalization (RFC 4518 string prep — already in pkix-path).
- CSR parsing (not a verifier crate concern).
- Public Suffix List enforcement (eTLD blocking) — out, deliberately. Callers who need it pull in their own PSL crate. webpki makes this choice; we follow.
- Anything that requires chain context or trust-anchor knowledge.

## Acceptance

- Crate compiles in workspace (`cargo build --workspace`).
- Crate compiles standalone with no_std (`cargo build -p pkix-identity --no-default-features`).
- All public API declared with `NotYetImplemented` stubs.
- AGENTS.md `## What this is` section updated to include `pkix-identity` in the adjacent-crates list.
- Workspace tests still pass (`cargo test --workspace`).
- `pkix-identity/README.md` includes the scope-discipline block above.
- CHANGELOG entry in `pkix-identity/CHANGELOG.md` for v0.1.0.

## What this unblocks

After scaffold lands, `.11` fills in `verify_dns_name` body + ships `verify_tls_server` wrapper in pkix-chain. `.12` fills in `verify_mailbox` body + ships `verify_smime_signer`/`verify_smime_recipient` wrappers.
